From f26f995d96597a4fbd3979851f8455a7925dde4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 03:48:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Meta ad set/ad level breakdown and age/gender/country
 audience reporting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AUDIT_REPORT.md flagged both as missing (High). New on-demand Graph API
fetchers (meta-breakdowns.ts) and orchestration layer
(meta-breakdowns-live.ts) reuse the existing live-pull cache/multi-
connection-merge/partial-failure pattern from meta-live.ts. Wired into
the shared AdsReport component (channel-page.tsx) as four new tables —
Ad sets, Ads, Audience by age & gender, Audience by country — gated to
provider === "meta" in live mode, so they automatically show up on the
internal dashboard, the client portal, and public share links alike.

Ad sets/ads are capped to the top 50 by spend in the UI (not capped
server-side, unlike the top-25 country breakdown) to avoid an unbounded
table on large accounts. Entity status (active/paused) is intentionally
left off ad set/ad rows — Meta's insights endpoint doesn't return it and
fetching it would mean a second paginated call per level.

